Copyright 2026 Lasimeri

The prediction method, and the code that carries it (the prompt layouts in
src/prompt.rs, the decode plan in src/engine.rs, the judge in src/judge.rs,
the readout's exact path in src/readout.rs, the wire types in
src/protocol.rs and the answer math in src/score.rs), are ported from
Intel-Phi-Jev (https://github.com/Lasimeri/Intel-Phi-Jev, its `xks` and
ARTICHOKE engine), which began as an import of jev-rs by Yijun Yu and
contributors (https://github.com/yijunyu/jev-rs), used under the MIT license
or the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE).

The confidence formulas in src/score.rs and their test cases follow
TypeSafe AI's system-one-adapter (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 TypeSafe
AI).

The request files under examples/ are Intel-Phi-Jev's examples.

llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, MIT License) is fetched at
build time into third_party/ and linked statically; it is not part of this
repository.

